course: dictionary
lesson: 15878
title: Unimpeded
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Unimpeded means not blocked or slowed down, so it is free to move or happen. The word is made of un-, which means "not", and impeded, which means "got in the way of". So unimpeded means "not got in the way of". Read the clues around it: «The river flowed unimpeded through the valley, with no rocks or dams to stop it.»
explain: The words no rocks or dams tell you what could have blocked the water. Nothing did, so the water flowed freely. Unimpeded is the opposite of blocked. To check, swap in your meaning: "The river flowed freely through the valley" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: You will meet unimpeded mostly in formal writing and exam texts, such as «unimpeded access» to a building, which means people can get in with nothing stopping them. «She had an unimpeded view of the stage» means nothing was in front of her eyes.
fact: Unimpeded means not blocked or slowed down.
fact: The prefix un- means "not", and impede means "to get in the way of".
fact: «An unimpeded view» means a clear view with nothing in the way.
fact: «Flow unimpeded» means to flow freely, like water or light passing through clean glass without being stopped.
fact: In everyday speech, people say "with nothing in the way" instead of unimpeded.
exercise: «The river flowed unimpeded through the valley.» What does unimpeded mean? | Very deep and dark | *Not blocked, flowing freely | Dried up completely | Frozen solid
exercise: «Our class had unimpeded access to the library all week.» What does unimpeded access mean? | Access only for teachers | A library card that costs money | Access that is closed until Monday | *Access with nothing stopping you
exercise: «The light passed unimpeded through the clean glass.» What is the best meaning here? | It bounced off and went back out | *It went through without being blocked | It was too weak to see | It turned dark and cold
test: «Dad's car had an unimpeded view of the road ahead.» What does unimpeded show? | Dad had no car | The view was blocked by fog | The road was closed | *The view was clear, with nothing in the way
test: Which phrase means the same as "flow unimpeded"? | *Flow freely with nothing in the way | Flow only at night | Flow backwards up the hill | Stop completely
exam: Which word best completes the sentence? «The buses ran ____ after the road works ended.» | famished | glum | curt | *unimpeded
